  "aiContextParagraph": "President Prabowo Subianto has reiterated Indonesia's diplomatic stance, advocating for open and fair engagement within the international system. This follows his high-profile visit to China, where the two nations finalized four strategic business and government agreements estimated to reach a total value exceeding Rp 1,300 trillion. Beyond the developments with China, the Indonesian government has actively pursued diverse international partnerships, including discussions regarding semiconductor industry investments with South Korean representatives and collaborations on maritime human resource development. Domestically, various sectors have also engaged in cooperative efforts, including business deals between regional entrepreneurs and academic partnerships between institutions like UNG and IPDN. Meanwhile, military cooperation remains a focal point, as evidenced by recent training agreements between the Indonesian Air Force and the Republic of Singapore Air Force to share exercise zones for fighter aircraft.",
